1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT João Lopes  was born in Mosteiros, São Miguel, Açores.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: 1 - João Lopes, of Mosteiross, man of much strenght as well as the sons and the daughter (See Frutuoso in Saudades da Terra Book IV Chapter VIII and Chap.) III § and in book VII and Capter) XVIII § XIV).
2 CONT It ignores with whom he married, but these are his children:
2 CONT
2 CONT João married someone.
2 CONT
2 CONT His child was:
2 CONT
2 CONT 22	i.	Manuel Lopes.  Manuel married Maria de Oliveira, daughter of Afonso Oliveira and Solanda Lopes, about 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT 46.  Afonso Oliveira , son of Diogo Oliveira Vasconcelos and Maria Esteves, was born in Beja, Portugal and died after 5 Jul 1586 in Mosteiros, São Miguel, Açores.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes:
2 CONT He ordered To construct a Hermitage (Chapel )in  Mosteiros, Ermida de São Lazaro) Saint Lazarus about 1510. He made a promise if his generation did not have such illness as he did that he would construct this Hermitage and thus he
2 CONC  did. And it is said that today Mass is still celebrated for the soul of this family. And to relate it seems thatAfonso de Oliveira was Buried in his Land because of being a Leper the law did not permit that Leper to be burried in
2 CONC  Public Cemetery, and in this land today a rock with across is found there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Afonso married Solanda Lopes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes: DA DESCENDÊNCIA DE DIOGO DE OLIVEIRA DE VASCONCELOS
2 CONT (The Descendancy of Diogo de Oliveira de Vasconcelos)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 10) Afonso de Oliveira (No. 2 § 3. º)
2 CONT Solanda Lopes, wife of Alfonso de Oliveira, linked by testament on 7.5.1586 to Manuel de Oliveira Vasconcelos her son, which was opened and expanded in 1589, when she died in Mosteiros.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this testament talks about his granddaughter Ines de Oliveira, daughter of Manuel Lopes, and the son Amador de Oliveira and son Alexo de Oliveira.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the process of accounts of the institution their son Manuel de Oliveira Vasconcelos, Manuel de Oliveira or Velho in 1590, after his son João Oliveira de Vasconcelos who administered the years (1608-1610); in 1626 João Pavão (Ro
2 CONC iz) Rodrigues, new administrator, in 1631 the same João RoizOliveira and John or João de Teve Carneiro, as heirs of the old administrator (sic) João Oliveira de Vasconcelos;
2 CONT Note No. 7 of Chapter # 78. º).
2 CONT
2 CONT The child from this marriage was:
2 CONT
2 CONT 23	i.	Maria de Oliveira.  Maria married Manuel Lopes, son of João Lopes and Unknown, about 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT 47.  Solanda Lopes , daughter of Afonso Anes Columbreiro O Mouro and Inês Martins, died after 1586 in Mosteiros, São Miguel, Açores.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: Saudades da Terrar 4th book
2 CONT Did last Will and Testament 7 de Maio 1586
2 CONT
2 CONT Made a Will on the 7th of May 1586
2 CONT
2 CONT Solanda married Afonso Oliveira.
